From 338f3db89706872157e4afa6ca9f22234c4dffb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:21:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: RPC work queue, resident memory and open file
 descriptors

A node refusing RPCs with "work queue depth exceeded", growing in
memory, or running out of file descriptors showed it only in logs or
from outside the process.

- fullnode_rpc_work_queue_depth and fullnode_rpc_work_in_flight: the
  HTTP coroutine pool's queued and in-flight counts, mirrored into gauges
  where they change (under the pool's mutex, already held);
  fullnode_rpc_work_queue_capacity (-rpcworkqueue), set when the pool
  starts; fullnode_rpc_work_suspended (long polls holding no worker,
  where the pool already counts them); and
  fullnode_rpc_work_queue_rejected_total at the 503 refusal.
- process_resident_memory_bytes, process_virtual_memory_bytes,
  process_open_fds and process_max_fds, the standard Prometheus names
  (no fullnode_ namespace, like process_start_time_seconds), read at
  scrape time by metrics::ReadProcessStats: /proc/self/statm and
  /proc/self/fd on Linux, task_info and proc_pidinfo on macOS,
  getrlimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE) for the limit. Figures a platform does not
  give are left out of the update (Windows: none).

process_cpu_seconds_total is not added: its value is fractional and the
registry's counters are integers.

Cardinality: nine series, no labels.

Hot paths: the work queue gauges add a relaxed store per enqueue,
dequeue and completion, under the lock those paths already hold. The
process figures cost a few system calls per rendering (at most one a
second), off every node path.

Evidence:
- metrics_tests/process_stats: resident and virtual sizes are read, and
  opening a file raises the open descriptor count by exactly one (macOS
  here).
- interface_metrics_runtime.py: process figures plausible (resident >
  1 MB, virtual >= resident, open fds > 10 and <= the limit); capacity
  is -rpcworkqueue=7; the scrape is in flight; a long poll is counted
  suspended, then not; with -rpcworkqueue=1 -rpcthreads=1, four
  concurrent long polls get at least one 503, and the rejected counter
  equals the refusals seen. Passed twice.

Not tested: the queue depth gauge above 0 (it is transient between
enqueue and a worker picking the request up); the Linux /proc readers
(this machine is macOS).

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Resolve integration context by retaining the incoming purposeful change together with existing shared/native consumers; exact old/new patch and file inventory is retained in owner-adaptations.json. No authored purpose or removed downstream behavior restored.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.
